You're right; I overthought the test coverage here. However, I'd suggest keeping one template instantiation test like this:

``` cc
template <typename T> struct Vector {
  typedef T type __attribute__((ext_vector_type(4)));
};

Vector<E> enum_vector; // expected-note {{in instantiation of template class 'GH225037::Vector<GH225037::E>' requested here}}
Vector<int> int_vector;
```

This would check that an enum element type is rejected when the template is instantiated. Would that make sense?

